selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/index.html#module-pyskyfire.injector\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.injector<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.injector\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Injectors: element sets on a face, and the flow from each feed through them.</p><p>Each element type is its own class. <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ImpingingElement</span></code> is the first:\njets aimed at a common point, which covers like and unlike doublets, triplets\nand pentads. Holes are <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Orifice</span></code> objects, so sizing,\ndischarge coefficients, choking and cavitation come from <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/index.html#module-pyskyfire.ducts\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts</span></code></a>.\nThis subpackage depends on <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/index.html#module-pyskyfire.ducts\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts</span></code></a> and <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/index.html#module-pyskyfire.thermo\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo</span></code></a>\nonly; the engine network adapts it through\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">InjectorBlock</span></code>.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/injector/ElementSet.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.ElementSet\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.ElementSet\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.injector.injector.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ElementSet</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">element</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">r</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">theta</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">orientation</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>One element type repeated at supplied face positions.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/index.html#module-pyskyfire.ducts\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.ducts<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.ducts\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Duct hydraulics shared by cooling channels, piping and manifolds.</p><p>This subpackage contains shared path geometry, explicit pipe hydraulics,\nannular ducts, orifices and orifice plates, and volute and collector manifolds. It depends only on <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/common/index.html#module-pyskyfire.common\" title=\"pyskyfire.common\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.common</span></code></a> for\nplanar section primitives and friction correlations and <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/index.html#module-pyskyfire.thermo\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.thermo</span></code></a> for fluid state records,\nand it does not import from <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/index.html#module-pyskyfire.regen\" title=\"pyskyfire.regen\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen</span></code></a> or <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/network/index.html#module-pyskyfire.network\" title=\"pyskyfire.network\"><code class=\"xref py py-mod docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.network</span></code></a>,\nso cooling channels, turbopump hardware and engine-network adapters can all\ndepend on it without a cycle.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/orifice/Orifice.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Orifice</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">area</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">cd</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">hydraulic_diameter</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">length</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>A short restriction discharging into a large volume.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>Use <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.circular\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.circular\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">circular()</span></code></a>, <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.annular\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.annular\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">annular()</span></code></a> or <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.slot\" title=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.slot\"><code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">slot()</span></code></a> for those shapes.\nThe generic constructor takes any area, so an effective area quoted as\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Cd\u00b7A</span></code> can be given as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Orifice(area=CdA,</span> <span class=\"pre\">cd=1.0)</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/impinging/ImpingingElement.html#pyskyfire.injector.impinging.ImpingingElement\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.injector.impinging.ImpingingElement\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.injector.impinging.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ImpingingElement</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">jets</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">impingement_height</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/element/Element.html#pyskyfire.injector.element.Element\" title=\"pyskyfire.injector.element.Element\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.injector.element.Element</span></code></a></p><p>Jets drilled to meet at a point <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">impingement_height</span></code> above the face.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"orifices.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Size and solve orifices<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#size-and-solve-orifices\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.ducts</span></code> has two restrictions described by a flow area and a\ndischarge coefficient:</p>", "a[href=\"#impinging-elements\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Impinging elements<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#impinging-elements\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>An <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ImpingingElement</span></code> is a set of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Jet</span></code>s aimed at one point a height above the\nface. Each jet names its feed, its hole, its inclination from the chamber axis\nand its azimuth around the element centre:</p>", "a[href=\"#checks\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Checks<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#checks\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>These cover what the injector owns: the narrowest web between hole outlines\non the face, overlapping holes, the room between the holes and the wall\n(<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">wall_clearance</span></code>), how far the impingement points sit inside it\n(<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">target_clearance</span></code>, zero for jets aimed at the wall on purpose), and the\nshortest hole relative to its diameter. Whether an\nelement sits where it should (clear of a baffle, say) is for whatever placed it.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/injector/Injector.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.Injector.checks\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.Injector.checks\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">checks</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">chamber_radius</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/injector/InjectorChecks.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.InjectorChecks\" title=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.InjectorChecks\"><span class=\"pre\">InjectorChecks</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p>Layout checks: webs between holes, holes and targets against the wall, hole L/D.</p><p>Hole outlines on the face are taken as circles of the\n<code class=\"xref py py-attr docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">InjectorHoles.footprint</span></code> radius, which is conservative for an\ninclined hole\u2019s ellipse.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#in-an-engine-network\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">In an engine network<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#in-an-engine-network\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Each feed is one block, from its plenum station to a face station:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/injector/Injector.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.Injector.solve\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.Injector.solve\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">solve</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">conditions</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/library/collections.abc.html#collections.abc.Mapping\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">Mapping</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">p_face</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">oxidizer</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">()</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span> <span class=\"sig-return\"><span class=\"sig-return-icon\">\u2192</span> <span class=\"sig-return-typehint\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/injector/InjectorResult.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.InjectorResult\" title=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.InjectorResult\"><span class=\"pre\">InjectorResult</span></a></span></span></dt><dd><p>Every feed at its operating point, discharging into a face at <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">p_face</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#sizing-holes\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Sizing holes<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#sizing-holes\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Size each hole for its share of its feed\u2019s flow at the feed\u2019s pressure drop:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/injector/InjectorResult.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.InjectorResult.mixture_ratio\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.InjectorResult.mixture_ratio\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">property</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">mixture_ratio</span></span><span class=\"property\"><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span></dt><dd><p>Overall oxidizer over fuel mass flow, NaN without a named oxidizer.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/network/blocks/InjectorBlock.html#pyskyfire.network.blocks.InjectorBlock\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.network.blocks.InjectorBlock\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.network.blocks.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">InjectorBlock</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">st_in</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">st_out</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#str\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">str</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">injector</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">feed</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">fluid</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">FluidBlock</span></code></p><p>Engine-network adapter for one feed of an <code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Injector</span></code>.</p><p>An injector with several feeds (a main fuel plenum, a film ring and an\noxidizer plenum, say) takes one block per feed, each with its own plenum\nstation. The block hands the plenum station and its mass flow to\n<code class=\"xref py py-meth docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Injector.solve_feed()</span></code> and emits the face station and the\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">dp_&lt;name&gt;</span></code> pressure drop from plenum to face.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>The flow is adiabatic, so the face station carries the plenum enthalpy.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.add\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.add\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">add</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">component</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">transform</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">position</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rotation</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">parent</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">anchor</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">attach_to</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">tags</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">()</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/orifice/Orifice.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.circular\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.circular\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">circular</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">diameter</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">cd</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">length</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>A round hole of <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">diameter</span></code> [m].</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#design-and-solve-an-injector\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Design and solve an injector<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#design-and-solve-an-injector\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>An injector in <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.injector</span></code> is a list of element sets. Each set is one\nelement type repeated at face positions you supply. Holes are\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ducts.Orifice</span></code> objects, so sizing, discharge coefficients, choking and\ncavitation work as in <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"orifices.html\"><span class=\"doc\">Size and solve orifices</span></a>.</p><p>The injector frame is the scene frame: the face is the plane x = 0, the\nchamber lies towards +x, and a position <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">(r,</span> <span class=\"pre\">\u03b8)</span></code> on the face is\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">y</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">r</span> <span class=\"pre\">cos</span> <span class=\"pre\">\u03b8</span></code>, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">z</span> <span class=\"pre\">=</span> <span class=\"pre\">r</span> <span class=\"pre\">sin</span> <span class=\"pre\">\u03b8</span></code>.</p>", "a[href=\"#solving\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Solving<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#solving\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>All the holes on one feed share its plenum and discharge to the same face, so\nthey run at one mass flux. A feed is exactly one orifice with the summed area\nand <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Cd\u00b7A</span></code> (<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">injector.equivalent_orifice(feed)</span></code>), and each hole takes the\nshare of the flow its own <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">Cd\u00b7A</span></code> sets.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">solve</span></code> takes one <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">FeedCondition</span></code> per feed. A condition with a pressure finds\nthe flow; one with a mass flow finds the plenum pressure. The two can be\nmixed:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/impinging/Jet.html#pyskyfire.injector.impinging.Jet\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.injector.impinging.Jet\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.injector.impinging.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Jet</span></span></dt><dd><p>One jet of an impinging element.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/injector_viz/InjectorComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.injector_viz.InjectorComponent\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.injector_viz.InjectorComponent\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.injector_viz.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">InjectorComponent</span></span></dt><dd><p>Display the wetted bores of an injector\u2019s holes, coloured by feed.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>Only wetted surface is drawn as hardware. A hole\u2019s bore runs back from the\nface along its axis for the orifice\u2019s <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">length</span></code>, or two diameters where\nno length is given, and ends where it meets the face plane. The arrows\nare drawn in grey, without fields, as annotation. The <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">face</span></code> anchor sits\non the axis at the face, pointing into the chamber.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#placing-elements\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Placing elements<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#placing-elements\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Positions are plain arrays, from any source. Rings take a few lines of numpy:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/injector/Injector.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.Injector\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.Injector\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.injector.injector.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Injector</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">element_sets</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Element sets on a face, and the hydraulics of the feeds that supply them.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/injector/FeedCondition.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.FeedCondition\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.FeedCondition\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.injector.injector.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">FeedCondition</span></span></dt><dd><p>The operating point of one feed.</p><p>Give the plenum <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">temperature</span></code> [K], the <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">fluid</span></code> (anything\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/thermo/eos/index.html#pyskyfire.thermo.eos.as_equation_of_state\" title=\"pyskyfire.thermo.eos.as_equation_of_state\"><code class=\"xref py py-func docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">as_equation_of_state()</span></code></a> reads), and either the\nplenum <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pressure</span></code> [Pa], to find the flow it drives, or the\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">mass_flow</span></code> [kg/s], to find the pressure it needs.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/ducts/orifice/Orifice.html#pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.sized\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.ducts.orifice.Orifice.sized\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">classmethod</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">sized</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">mass_flow</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">inlet_state</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">dp</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">fluid</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">cd</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">length</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>The round hole that passes <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">mass_flow</span></code> with a pressure drop <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">dp</span></code>.</p><p>See <code class=\"xref py py-func docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">required_area()</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/index.html#module-pyskyfire.viz\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">pyskyfire.viz<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#module-pyskyfire.viz\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><h2>Submodules<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#submodules\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.save_html\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene.save_html\">\n<span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">save_html</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">path</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/injector/InjectorChecks.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.InjectorChecks\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.InjectorChecks\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.injector.injector.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">InjectorChecks</span></span></dt><dd><p>What the injector can check about its own layout, reported not enforced.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">min_web</span></code> is the narrowest ligament between two hole outlines on the\nface [m], between holes in sets <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">min_web_sets</span></code>; <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">overlaps</span></code> counts\npairs whose outlines intersect. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">outer_radius</span></code> is how far the\noutermost hole outline reaches from the axis, and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">target_radius</span></code> the\nfurthest any jet\u2019s target lies from it [m]. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">wall_clearance</span></code> is the\nchamber radius less <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">outer_radius</span></code>: room between the holes and the\nwall. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">target_clearance</span></code> is the chamber radius less <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">target_radius</span></code>:\nzero where a jet is aimed at the wall on purpose, as a film-cooling jet\nis, and negative where a target lies beyond it. Both are NaN without a\nchamber radius. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">min_length_to_diameter</span></code> is the shortest hole relative\nto its diameter.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#feeds\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Feeds<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#feeds\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>A feed is whatever supplies a hole. It can be feed hardware, such as a\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ducts.Manifold</span></code>, or a name where the hardware is not modelled yet. Feeds\ncompare as dictionary keys, so hardware objects compare by identity. Holes\non the same feed share one plenum; holes on different feeds, such as a film\nring supplied separately from the main plenum, never combine.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/scene/Scene.html#pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.scene.Scene\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.scene.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Scene</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">title</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'Pyskyfire</span> <span class=\"pre\">3D'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">color_by</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">clim</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">show_axes</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Assemble components for desktop or standalone HTML display.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">anchor</span></code> names the added component\u2019s local anchor; <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">attach_to</span></code> is a\nworld-space Anchor. Attachment mates their outward x axes in opposition.\nIt is a one-time placement calculation, with no fluid-network constraints.\nExplicit placement and anchor placement are mutually exclusive.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">tags</span></code> labels the added node, a string or an iterable of them. Nodes\nsharing a tag appear together as one group in the HTML viewer, so a\ngrouping written into the script survives regenerating the results.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">show_axes</span></code> adds a corner orientation triad marking the scene axes\n(x red, y green, z blue). It is an orientation cue only, not a measuring\ngrid: it carries no ticks and does not indicate the origin or scale.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/injector/injector/InjectorResult.html#pyskyfire.injector.injector.InjectorResult\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.injector.injector.InjectorResult\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.injector.injector.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">InjectorResult</span></span></dt><dd><p>Every feed and set at one operating point, into a face at <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">p_face</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/injector_viz/index.html#pyskyfire.viz.injector_viz.plot_injector_face\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.viz.injector_viz.plot_injector_face\">\n<span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.viz.injector_viz.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">plot_injector_face</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">injector</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">face_radius</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">colors</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">labels</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">title</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>The injector seen from the chamber, in millimetres.</p><p>Each hole\u2019s outline on the face is drawn in its feed\u2019s colour, with its\njet projected onto the face as a line to the impingement point, where a\ngrey dot marks where the jets meet. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">face_radius</span></code> adds the chamber wall\nas a grey circle. Hovering a hole shows its set, feed and diameter.</p><p>Parameters are as for <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/viz/injector_viz/InjectorComponent.html#pyskyfire.viz.injector_viz.InjectorComponent\" title=\"pyskyfire.viz.injector_viz.InjectorComponent\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">InjectorComponent</span></code></a>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#viewing-it\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Viewing it<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#viewing-it\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The scene draws wetted surface only: each hole\u2019s bore, one colour per feed,\nending where it meets the face plate. Hole terminations such as counterbores\nor chamfers are not modelled yet. <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">show_impingement=True</span></code> adds grey arrows\nfrom each hole to its impingement point; they are annotation, not hardware.\nWith a <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">result</span></code>, each bore carries <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">hole_mass_flow</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">jet_velocity</span></code> fields\nto colour by.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">examples/injector/injector_report.py</span></code> puts this together: a LOX/methane\ninjector with a separately fed film ring, sized, rounded to drills, and\nrated both ways.</p>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
